Brainstorming & Ideation Phase
LegalEase: AI-Powered Legal Document Generator

Brainstorming & Ideation Phase

1. Introduction

The Brainstorming & Ideation Phase is the first major stage of the LegalEase project. In this phase, the project idea is discussed, problems are identified, possible solutions are explored, and the main features of the system are finalized.

LegalEase is proposed as an AI-powered legal document generator that helps users create structured legal documents by entering simple information about their requirements. The system aims to make basic document preparation easier, faster, and more accessible.

> Important: LegalEase is intended as a document-generation and drafting assistance tool, not a replacement for a qualified lawyer or legal advice.




---

2. Problem Identification

Creating a legal document manually can be difficult for people who are unfamiliar with legal terminology and document formats.

Common problems identified during brainstorming include:

Users may not know the correct format of a legal document.

Legal terminology can be difficult to understand.

Preparing documents manually takes considerable time.

Small formatting mistakes can affect the quality of a document.

People may not know what information should be included.

Finding suitable templates for different documents can be difficult.

Professional legal assistance may not always be immediately accessible for simple drafting tasks.

Users may need to repeatedly edit and format documents.


These problems created the need for a simple digital solution.


---

3. Proposed Solution

The proposed solution is LegalEase, an AI-powered web application that assists users in generating draft legal documents.

The user provides basic information through a simple interface. The system processes the information and generates a structured draft based on the selected document type.

Basic working idea:

User Input → Document Type Selection → AI Processing → Draft Generation → Review → Download

The generated document should be treated as a draft for review, especially for important legal matters.


---

4. Brainstorming of Features

During the brainstorming process, several features were considered.

A. Document Type Selection

Users can select the type of document they want to generate.

Possible categories include:

Rental agreement draft

Leave/permission letter

Affidavit-style draft

Declaration

Authorization letter

Complaint/representation draft

Employment-related letters

Notice drafts

Application letters

General agreements


The exact document types can be expanded later.


---

B. Simple User Input

Instead of asking users to write complicated legal language, LegalEase can provide a form containing simple questions.

For example:

Full name

Address

Date

Purpose of the document

Names of involved parties

Important terms or conditions

Duration

Additional information


This makes the system easier for beginners to use.


---

C. AI-Based Draft Generation

The main idea of the project is to use AI to convert the user's information into a properly structured document.

For example:

User Input:

> "I want a rental agreement for one year."



The system can collect the required details and generate a structured draft containing sections such as:

Parties involved

Property details

Rental period

Rent

Responsibilities

Terms and conditions

Signatures



---

D. Document Preview

Before downloading, users should be able to preview the generated document.

This helps users:

Check the information

Identify missing details

Review the wording

Make corrections

Confirm the document structure



---

E. Edit and Regenerate

The user should be able to modify information and generate an updated version.

For example:

Old rent: ₹10,000
New rent: ₹12,000

After changing the information, the user can regenerate the draft.


---

F. Download and Export

The generated document can be provided in formats such as:

PDF

DOCX

TXT


The exact formats depend on the project's implementation.


---

5. AI Integration Idea

The AI component is the core of LegalEase.

The AI can be used to:

1. Understand the user's requirements.


2. Identify the selected document type.


3. Organize the provided information.


4. Generate appropriate sections.


5. Produce clear and professional draft language.


6. Identify potentially missing information.


7. Explain difficult terminology in simpler language.



The AI should not invent important facts supplied by the user.


